    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive strategy for July 21st hinges on exploiting favorable matchups against a slate of mediocre arms, specifically targeting the Lorenzen start. **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) serves as our cornerstone play today; he benefits from a highly favorable park factor and a \"Slow SP Delivery\" tag that pushes his SB upside into elite territory against the opposing starter. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Nasim Nunez** (71.66) are equally critical to our core production, both seeing significant statistical boosts from the favorable park and the vulnerability of the opposing staff. While **Heliot Ramos** (67.31) and **Drake Baldwin** (67.13) provide high-floor contributions from the top of the order, it is the combination of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**\u2019s platoon advantage and the aggressive baserunning environment for our middle infielders that gives us the highest potential to manufacture runs in a 5x5 format.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved keeping **Miguel Vargas** (55.79) on the bench. Despite his excellent xwOBA projection of 0.399 and a favorable matchup against Rocker, his efficiency score fell just short of our starting threshold when compared against the stability of **Jacob Wilson** (65.19) and the platoon upside of our other infielders. We are closely monitoring the lineup status for **Jacob Wilson**, as any late change to his confirmed batting order could shift the value proposition; however, his current efficiency against the lefty starter remains superior to the bench alternatives. Conversely, we are exercising caution with **Kyle Tucker** (53.52) today. Facing a pitcher of Wheeler\u2019s caliber inherently suppresses his offensive ceiling, and while he is too valuable to sit, his score reflects the undeniable risk of squaring off against an elite arm. We will rely on the volume and speed upside of **Nasim Nunez** and **Jackson Merrill** to offset any potential stagnation from the harder matchups at the bottom of the order.",
